1
00:00:01,490 --> 00:00:03,270
My name is Echidna...

2
00:00:03,800 --> 00:00:07,720
Or perhaps you would know me 
better as the Witch of Greed?

3
00:00:12,090 --> 00:00:15,320
Please, it hurts to see you 
look so alarmed by me.

4
00:00:15,320 --> 00:00:18,980
Despite who I am, I'm still a 
tender young maiden, you know.

5
00:00:18,980 --> 00:00:20,220
Sorry, but...

6
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:23,980
There's no way I'm <i>not</i> going to 
be alarmed when you tell me

7
00:00:23,980 --> 00:00:25,540
you're the Witch of Greed the moment we meet.

8
00:00:25,910 --> 00:00:27,040
I see.

9
00:00:27,690 --> 00:00:29,000
That's a fair point.

10
00:00:34,840 --> 00:00:36,430
What is this place?

11
00:00:36,430 --> 00:00:38,840
I was in some dark ruins just a moment ago!

12
00:00:38,840 --> 00:00:40,740
When did you move me?!

13
00:00:40,740 --> 00:00:43,580
Unfortunately, you're mistaken.

14
00:00:43,580 --> 00:00:46,640
You weren't physically moved anywhere.

15
00:00:47,100 --> 00:00:49,760
You were merely invited to my tea party.

16
00:00:49,760 --> 00:00:51,030
Tea party?

17
00:00:51,660 --> 00:00:53,360
A witch's tea party.

18
00:00:54,540 --> 00:00:56,710
Are you going to stand there forever?

19
00:00:57,100 --> 00:01:00,370
Why don't you at least sit down 
before the tea gets cold?

20
00:01:01,830 --> 00:01:02,790
Oh, damn it!

21
00:01:03,130 --> 00:01:04,960
All right, fine!

22
00:01:07,540 --> 00:01:09,410
You're awfully brave,

23
00:01:09,410 --> 00:01:11,700
gulping down tea served by a witch in one gulp.

24
00:01:11,700 --> 00:01:14,500
Hah! If you really wanted to kill me,

25
00:01:14,500 --> 00:01:16,830
I'd be a pile of ash the very next instant.

26
00:01:16,830 --> 00:01:19,690
What's this tea, anyway? It's not bad,
 but it's not good, either.

27
00:01:19,690 --> 00:01:21,760
It's something that's produced here.

28
00:01:21,760 --> 00:01:23,430
To put it bluntly, 
it's a body fluid of mine.

29
00:01:23,430 --> 00:01:26,300
What the hell did you just make me drink?!

30
00:01:26,880 --> 00:01:29,060
You truly are a fascinating individual.

31
00:01:29,600 --> 00:01:32,400
You're standing right here in 
front of me as if it's normal.

32
00:01:32,660 --> 00:01:36,770
Hah! You think you're so pretty that a 
normal person's eyes would fall out?

33
00:01:36,770 --> 00:01:42,190
I'll have you know that my eyes are blessed 
throughout the day by the prettiest girl alive!

34
00:01:42,190 --> 00:01:44,070
So no matter how many times I look at you,

35
00:01:44,070 --> 00:01:47,980
I'm not going to see you as particularly pretty.

36
00:01:47,980 --> 00:01:51,360
No, most normal people vomit 
when they stand before me.

37
00:01:51,360 --> 00:01:52,270
Funny, right?

38
00:01:52,270 --> 00:01:53,920
There's nothing funny about that!

39
00:01:55,050 --> 00:01:56,840
What is it you want with me?

40
00:01:57,240 --> 00:01:58,700
Nothing, really.

41
00:01:58,700 --> 00:02:01,170
You came in here of your own accord.

42
00:02:01,170 --> 00:02:03,620
If you want to go back, I'll send you back...

43
00:02:04,370 --> 00:02:05,980
But are you sure that's what you want?

44
00:02:06,340 --> 00:02:07,230
Huh?

45
00:02:07,520 --> 00:02:10,890
An opportunity to talk to the Witch of Greed

46
00:02:10,890 --> 00:02:14,860
is not something that just anyone, 
other than you, can earn.

47
00:02:15,300 --> 00:02:17,560
The only requirement to have a dialogue

48
00:02:17,560 --> 00:02:19,290
is for both of us to exist.

49
00:02:19,670 --> 00:02:22,070
Let's remove everything 
unnecessary from the picture.

50
00:02:22,590 --> 00:02:24,330
All we need is our words.

51
00:02:24,500 --> 00:02:28,660
Let me affirm all the desires, 
the curiosities, the greed,

52
00:02:28,660 --> 00:02:30,620
that you seek to satisfy with answers.

53
00:02:33,910 --> 00:02:37,340
Now, what would you like to ask me?

54
00:02:38,050 --> 00:02:40,260
About the Witch of Gluttony, Daphne,

55
00:02:40,470 --> 00:02:45,970
who created beasts that defied the will 
of God to save the world from starvation?

56
00:02:46,580 --> 00:02:48,600
About the Witch of Lust, Carmilla,

57
00:02:48,600 --> 00:02:54,100
who granted emotions to non-human beings 
in an attempt to fill the world with love?

58
00:02:54,560 --> 00:02:56,980
About the Witch of Wrath, Minerva,

59
00:02:56,980 --> 00:03:01,730
who struck people to heal them as she 
lamented the state of her war-torn world?

60
00:03:02,110 --> 00:03:03,860
About the Witch of Sloth, Sekhmet,

61
00:03:03,860 --> 00:03:10,070
who drove a dragon past the 
great waterfall just for a chance to rest?

62
00:03:10,070 --> 00:03:12,190
About the Witch of Pride, Typhon,

63
00:03:12,190 --> 00:03:16,000
who, out of youthful innocence and cruelty,
 judged criminals one after another?

64
00:03:16,770 --> 00:03:19,010
About the Witch of Greed, Echidna,

65
00:03:19,010 --> 00:03:22,750
the embodiment of the thirst for knowledge, 
who has done things she regrets

66
00:03:22,750 --> 00:03:25,390
even in the realm of death, all in 
pursuit of all types of knowledge?

67
00:03:25,960 --> 00:03:26,760
Or...

68
00:03:27,190 --> 00:03:29,480
The Witch of Envy, who killed 
all the other witches

69
00:03:29,480 --> 00:03:33,460
and used them as sustenance while she 
made the whole world her enemy—

70
00:03:33,460 --> 00:03:36,900
the most detestable of them all?

71
00:03:39,670 --> 00:03:40,610
Oh, darn.

72
00:03:41,630 --> 00:03:43,780
It looks like I've frightened you too much.

73
00:03:44,310 --> 00:03:47,500
Such is the nature of a witch. 
It's quite bothersome.

74
00:03:55,150 --> 00:03:57,640
Oh, that took less time than I thought.

75
00:03:57,640 --> 00:04:00,340
People who are compatible 
really do adapt quickly.

76
00:04:00,340 --> 00:04:01,880
What are you saying?

77
00:04:02,270 --> 00:04:03,880
That tea you drank?

78
00:04:03,880 --> 00:04:09,040
I used the Sloth Witch Factor on 
it to strengthen your resistance.

79
00:04:09,040 --> 00:04:11,890
Now you and I can talk at leisure.

80
00:04:12,380 --> 00:04:15,730
So... what would you like to ask me?

81
00:04:16,200 --> 00:04:18,280
You won't get away with this!

82
00:04:18,280 --> 00:04:21,000
What did you do to my body?!

83
00:04:21,000 --> 00:04:23,080
Please don't get the wrong idea.

84
00:04:23,080 --> 00:04:26,320
I didn't make you drink that tea with 
the intention of doing anything bad.

85
00:04:26,840 --> 00:04:29,030
In fact, I find your existence

86
00:04:29,230 --> 00:04:31,100
quite desirable.

87
00:04:32,270 --> 00:04:34,120
I'm a bit embarrassed, really.

88
00:04:34,440 --> 00:04:35,210
Huh?

89
00:04:37,040 --> 00:04:39,150
In these past few days, you killed the one

90
00:04:39,150 --> 00:04:42,170
who possessed the Sloth Witch Factor, correct?

91
00:04:42,570 --> 00:04:47,320
When he died, the Witch Factor 
chose you as its new dwelling.

92
00:04:47,690 --> 00:04:51,000
That's also why you were able to 
enter this graveyard unharmed.

93
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:53,730
Graveyard? Like... a tomb?

94
00:04:53,730 --> 00:04:54,100
Yes.

95
00:04:54,920 --> 00:04:59,210
This is the Witch's Graveyard, 
where my soul is held prisoner...

96
00:04:59,750 --> 00:05:01,030
The Sanctuary.

97
00:05:01,520 --> 00:05:03,570
You know where the Sanctuary is?!

98
00:05:04,720 --> 00:05:07,540
I don't have the experience 
to determine whether

99
00:05:07,540 --> 00:05:10,500
you're brave or just very bold...

100
00:05:10,500 --> 00:05:11,780
Don't make fun of me!

101
00:05:11,780 --> 00:05:15,620
So can I consider this... rather, the forest 
with the ruins where I was before...

102
00:05:15,620 --> 00:05:17,590
to be the Sanctuary?

103
00:05:17,590 --> 00:05:18,940
You're so mean...

104
00:05:19,400 --> 00:05:23,840
That's right. Just as you wanted, 
the Sanctuary is outside the ruins.

105
00:05:24,140 --> 00:05:26,660
So, what else would you like to as—

106
00:05:25,850 --> 00:05:28,650
And if I ask you, you'll let me back out, right?

107
00:05:29,770 --> 00:05:32,220
Sure... I can guarantee that.

108
00:05:32,940 --> 00:05:35,840
Hey, isn't there anything 
you want to ask me?

109
00:05:35,840 --> 00:05:40,680
Sorry, but I'd rather meet up with 
Emilia outside than talk to you.

110
00:05:40,680 --> 00:05:41,280
Huh?

111
00:05:42,040 --> 00:05:43,970
Y-You're kidding, right?!

112
00:05:43,970 --> 00:05:46,080
I'm the Witch of Greed!

113
00:05:46,080 --> 00:05:51,160
Powerful people from around the world have 
come to me in search of my knowledge!

114
00:05:51,160 --> 00:05:54,120
So, um... relax, okay?!
We can just relax and talk!

115
00:05:54,120 --> 00:05:56,750
I have knowledge about the truth 
of this world that nobody—

116
00:05:55,930 --> 00:05:56,750
Not interested.

117
00:05:56,750 --> 00:05:58,120
What?!

118
00:05:58,410 --> 00:06:02,760
I'll make time to chat over 
tea with you later, okay?

119
00:06:02,760 --> 00:06:05,570
You'd ask a dead woman... 
a witch, at that...

120
00:06:05,570 --> 00:06:09,550
to agree to that as if it 
were the simplest thing?

121
00:06:12,030 --> 00:06:14,520
I've never had a tea party like this.

122
00:06:15,360 --> 00:06:17,320
If you're really going back,

123
00:06:17,320 --> 00:06:19,310
I'll just take my compensation first.

124
00:06:19,310 --> 00:06:23,000
J-Just so you know, I'm broke beyond compare...

125
00:06:23,400 --> 00:06:26,250
Compensation for a witch doesn't mean money.

126
00:06:26,750 --> 00:06:29,500
What I desire from you is a vow.

127
00:06:30,170 --> 00:06:33,160
You will tell no one of what has 
transpired at this tea party.

128
00:06:33,160 --> 00:06:34,490
That is my condition.

129
00:06:34,890 --> 00:06:36,880
And, since you're here,

130
00:06:36,880 --> 00:06:39,010
I'll send you away with a souvenir.

131
00:06:39,010 --> 00:06:43,170
I will grant you the right to 
face the trial of the Sanctuary.

132
00:06:43,770 --> 00:06:45,800
The trial of the Sanctuary?

133
00:06:45,800 --> 00:06:47,770
You may not understand now,

134
00:06:48,140 --> 00:06:51,070
but once you learn where it is, 
you will realize its worth.

135
00:06:51,070 --> 00:06:55,390
What feelings will you have 
toward me when that happens?

136
00:06:56,120 --> 00:06:59,590
The mere thought gives me 
such beautiful expectations.

137
00:07:07,610 --> 00:07:10,660
You... really are a witch, aren't you?

138
00:07:10,660 --> 00:07:12,110
Yes, that's right.

139
00:07:12,780 --> 00:07:16,580
I'm a very, very evil magic user.

140
00:07:32,370 --> 00:07:34,520
Anyway, I need to get out of here,

141
00:07:34,520 --> 00:07:36,380
and back to Emilia-tan and Otto.

142
00:07:39,380 --> 00:07:40,640
<i>I feel like...</i>

143
00:07:41,090 --> 00:07:43,310
<i>someone said something to me.</i>

144
00:07:48,740 --> 00:07:49,610
Otto?!

145
00:07:49,610 --> 00:07:52,050
Look at you, just waltzing out of there!

146
00:07:52,050 --> 00:07:55,160
You've got some nerve, outsider!

147
00:07:55,160 --> 00:07:58,410
Is this like a magmarin laughing 
when it's full of holes?!

148
00:08:12,260 --> 00:08:13,600
Ow...

149
00:08:13,600 --> 00:08:15,350
Damn it! What the hell?

150
00:08:21,510 --> 00:08:23,180
What a tantalizing choice!

151
00:08:27,680 --> 00:08:29,730
That's a nice ground dragon ya got there.

152
00:08:32,140 --> 00:08:33,920
Wait, Patrasche!

153
00:08:38,060 --> 00:08:41,370
You're a real good-lookin' girl, ain't ya?

154
00:08:42,180 --> 00:08:44,170
I'm not gonna hurt ya!

155
00:08:44,170 --> 00:08:46,120
Just take a little nap!

156
00:08:50,970 --> 00:08:53,920
Better thank her for fightin' so hard for ya!

157
00:08:55,600 --> 00:08:56,510
Wait... Wait!

158
00:08:56,510 --> 00:09:00,470
I'm gonna throw you guys outta 
this forest half-dead...

159
00:09:00,790 --> 00:09:04,320
Just alive enough to swear you won't 
tell a soul about this place!

160
00:09:04,320 --> 00:09:07,100
You know Frederica, don't you?!

161
00:09:08,550 --> 00:09:11,980
Why the hell did I just hear that 
name from your nasty mouth?

162
00:09:12,200 --> 00:09:13,810
Why do you think?

163
00:09:13,810 --> 00:09:15,110
Just think about it!

164
00:09:15,110 --> 00:09:16,740
Thought about it. Don't know.

165
00:09:16,740 --> 00:09:18,710
I'll think after I bash your skull in!

166
00:09:17,890 --> 00:09:19,920
Quit jumping to conclusions without thinking!

167
00:09:19,920 --> 00:09:22,500
It's because we know her, too!

168
00:09:22,500 --> 00:09:23,320
Huh?

169
00:09:25,670 --> 00:09:28,090
I'm Garfiel.

170
00:09:28,090 --> 00:09:32,480
If you guys know her, you must've 
heard that name, right?

171
00:09:32,480 --> 00:09:33,510
Y-You're...

172
00:09:33,720 --> 00:09:37,480
How the hell did you know I have 
anything to do with Frederica?!

173
00:09:38,490 --> 00:09:40,260
Are you being serious right now?

174
00:09:41,520 --> 00:09:44,120
I just got beaten up for nothing.

175
00:09:44,120 --> 00:09:46,590
What am I supposed to do with this anger?

176
00:09:46,590 --> 00:09:48,240
You never shut up, do ya, trader?

177
00:09:48,240 --> 00:09:49,520
I apologized, didn't I?

178
00:09:49,520 --> 00:09:55,280
You call, "Hey, sorry, numbskull, 
I kinda jumped the gun," an apology?!

179
00:09:53,940 --> 00:09:57,360
Anyway, if you'd shown me that 
thing sooner, that woulda done it.

180
00:09:57,360 --> 00:09:59,870
Gotta act on a ganglion 
before ya think about it.

181
00:09:59,870 --> 00:10:01,090
Gangli... huh?

182
00:10:01,090 --> 00:10:04,580
Lookin' at that hair, I'm guessin' 
that's the famous Emilia-sama?

183
00:10:04,900 --> 00:10:08,240
The silver-haired half-devil 
that Roswaal's helpin' out.

184
00:10:08,240 --> 00:10:09,960
She's a half-elf!

185
00:10:09,960 --> 00:10:12,300
Don't you ever call her that again!

186
00:10:12,300 --> 00:10:16,510
Hey, look at that! Guess you can put 
some energy into yer voice after all!

187
00:10:16,810 --> 00:10:20,430
Wanna know how it feels to be a 
bazomazo bein' flung back an' forth?

188
00:10:20,430 --> 00:10:24,720
Uh, is there some sort of translation 
glitch happening between you and me?

189
00:10:24,720 --> 00:10:25,620
Huh?

190
00:10:28,560 --> 00:10:29,460
Emilia!

191
00:10:30,810 --> 00:10:32,700
I'm so glad you're okay!

192
00:10:32,700 --> 00:10:33,890
Subaru?

193
00:10:35,240 --> 00:10:36,280
Who are you?!

194
00:10:36,280 --> 00:10:38,960
Just so you know, I won't let 
you lay a finger on Subaru!

195
00:10:38,960 --> 00:10:40,270
Hang on, Emilia-tan!

196
00:10:40,270 --> 00:10:43,290
I appreciate it, but as a guy, I have 
mixed feelings about this! Really, I'm fine!

197
00:10:42,550 --> 00:10:44,350
I'm not gonna do anything.

198
00:10:44,350 --> 00:10:46,920
I don't want Ram givin' me hell later.

199
00:10:46,920 --> 00:10:47,760
Ram?

200
00:10:47,760 --> 00:10:49,540
This is Garfiel.

201
00:10:49,970 --> 00:10:53,460
Garfiel... The one Frederica told us about?

202
00:10:54,090 --> 00:10:58,670
Yeah, and he's showing us the 
way to the Sanctuary now.

203
00:10:58,670 --> 00:11:02,550
Ram and the villagers from 
Arlam are there... right?

204
00:11:02,910 --> 00:11:05,350
Don't wanna believe me? That's your call.

205
00:11:05,350 --> 00:11:08,140
Ain't no turnin' back now, though.

206
00:11:08,140 --> 00:11:10,310
We're already past the barrier.

207
00:11:11,240 --> 00:11:13,680
Then we're in the Sanctuary right now?

208
00:11:13,680 --> 00:11:15,580
C'mon, gimme a break.

209
00:11:15,580 --> 00:11:19,680
Weren't you asleep 'cause you 
got close to the barrier?

210
00:11:19,680 --> 00:11:20,570
The barrier?

211
00:11:21,180 --> 00:11:24,200
Come to think of it, when the stone glowed...

212
00:11:24,500 --> 00:11:26,350
It was at the exact same moment.

213
00:11:27,030 --> 00:11:29,540
So it was reacting to the barrier, then?

214
00:11:31,390 --> 00:11:34,570
But why did only Emilia-tan pass out?

215
00:11:34,570 --> 00:11:38,720
I mean, I got transported somewhere, but Otto—

216
00:11:39,590 --> 00:11:44,890
You know damn well why the barrier 
reacted to her and not you two.

217
00:11:45,190 --> 00:11:48,500
It's not just half-elves that thing reacts to.

218
00:11:48,500 --> 00:11:50,700
It works on me and a lot of others, too.

219
00:11:50,700 --> 00:11:51,800
That's 'cause...

220
00:11:52,530 --> 00:11:54,900
Because you have mixed blood, too?

221
00:11:56,140 --> 00:12:01,640
So the Sanctuary is a place where 
demihumans with mixed blood live?

222
00:12:01,640 --> 00:12:03,240
You guessed it!

223
00:12:03,240 --> 00:12:07,050
We welcome you, Emilia-sama, 
and your two escorts, too!

224
00:12:10,930 --> 00:12:14,780
Roswaal likes to go around 
callin' it the Sanctuary,

225
00:12:14,780 --> 00:12:18,620
but it ain't the kinda place 
that deserves such a nice name.

226
00:12:19,000 --> 00:12:22,070
Nothin' there but a hodgepodge of halfwits.

227
00:12:22,070 --> 00:12:24,890
It's just a dead-end testing ground.

228
00:12:27,080 --> 00:12:29,100
Um, where should...

229
00:12:30,220 --> 00:12:31,500
You're back?

230
00:12:31,880 --> 00:12:33,620
It took you long enough.

231
00:12:35,490 --> 00:12:36,660
Ram!

232
00:12:38,840 --> 00:12:40,900
I haven't a clue which Barusu you are,

233
00:12:40,900 --> 00:12:43,300
but I'm disappointed by how 
long it took you to get here.

234
00:12:43,300 --> 00:12:45,780
Ah, but I suppose I was a 
fool to expect more of you.

235
00:12:45,780 --> 00:12:49,630
If your story is that you "haven't 
a clue" who I am, stick to it!

236
00:12:49,630 --> 00:12:50,280
Hmph.

237
00:12:52,950 --> 00:12:55,590
Emilia-sama, I welcome you.

238
00:12:56,020 --> 00:12:58,140
Roswaal-sama is waiting inside.

239
00:12:58,140 --> 00:12:59,420
Allow me to show you the way.

240
00:13:00,010 --> 00:13:03,590
Garf, take the ground dragon and 
carriage somewhere suitable.

241
00:13:03,590 --> 00:13:06,030
Is that any way to treat me?

242
00:13:06,030 --> 00:13:07,640
That's just how I like it, though.

243
00:13:08,090 --> 00:13:09,960
Yo, cabbie, follow me.

244
00:13:09,960 --> 00:13:11,640
Are you referring to me?!

245
00:13:11,640 --> 00:13:13,500
That's the worst name you've called me yet!

246
00:13:13,500 --> 00:13:14,980
Also, I have to be alone with you?!

247
00:13:14,980 --> 00:13:16,220
I'll pick up what's left of you.

248
00:13:16,220 --> 00:13:18,460
Why am I being treated so roughly?!

249
00:13:18,880 --> 00:13:20,190
What're you talking about?

250
00:13:20,600 --> 00:13:22,350
When I was unconscious,

251
00:13:22,350 --> 00:13:25,110
Emilia only stayed safe because you were there.

252
00:13:25,760 --> 00:13:26,860
I'm grateful.

253
00:13:27,900 --> 00:13:29,200
O-Oh?

254
00:13:29,200 --> 00:13:32,580
W-Well, as long as you're appreciative...

255
00:13:33,070 --> 00:13:34,170
Right!

256
00:13:34,170 --> 00:13:35,430
He's too easy.

257
00:13:38,620 --> 00:13:39,170
What?

258
00:13:40,000 --> 00:13:42,930
Oh, just... wondering how you were doing.

259
00:13:43,430 --> 00:13:45,880
You remember what was going 
on the last time I saw you.

260
00:13:46,260 --> 00:13:48,230
I couldn't get in touch with you after that,

261
00:13:48,230 --> 00:13:50,890
and to be honest, I was really worried.

262
00:13:51,680 --> 00:13:55,110
As you can see, I am as 
lovely and healthy as ever.

263
00:13:55,680 --> 00:13:58,100
The villagers of Arlam are all safe, too.

264
00:13:58,500 --> 00:13:59,560
You can be at ease.

265
00:14:00,270 --> 00:14:01,330
I see...

266
00:14:01,770 --> 00:14:05,070
Yeah, that's... a real relief.

267
00:14:05,780 --> 00:14:06,860
A real relief.

268
00:14:11,180 --> 00:14:12,970
U-Um, listen...

269
00:14:15,480 --> 00:14:16,630
Hey, Ram...

270
00:14:17,360 --> 00:14:20,130
This really isn't a place 
to stand around and talk.

271
00:14:20,130 --> 00:14:21,850
Would you show us inside?

272
00:14:21,850 --> 00:14:23,100
Certainly.

273
00:14:28,760 --> 00:14:30,650
Subaru, are you all right?

274
00:14:30,650 --> 00:14:31,460
Yeah.

275
00:14:31,960 --> 00:14:34,860
I'm sorry for interrupting you, but...

276
00:14:35,470 --> 00:14:37,390
No, I get it.

277
00:14:37,390 --> 00:14:38,600
I just freaked out a little.

278
00:14:39,420 --> 00:14:42,660
For her to not even ask about Rem 
when all this is going on...

279
00:14:43,540 --> 00:14:44,730
I'm pathetic, huh?

280
00:14:48,630 --> 00:14:51,310
It's only natural to be scared.

281
00:14:51,310 --> 00:14:54,020
I'll never think that's pathetic.

282
00:14:55,010 --> 00:14:56,240
Let's go.

283
00:14:56,240 --> 00:15:00,290
We'll fix what happened to Rem, 
and everything else, too.

284
00:15:01,680 --> 00:15:02,830
Got it.

285
00:15:04,090 --> 00:15:05,490
No matter what happens,

286
00:15:05,490 --> 00:15:08,810
I'll be your meat shield and keep you safe.

287
00:15:10,840 --> 00:15:13,890
Ah, Emilia-sama and Subaru-kun.

288
00:15:14,350 --> 00:15:18,410
It feels like it's been so very 
long since I last saw you.

289
00:15:18,410 --> 00:15:21,350
I was going to slug you when 
I saw you again, but now...

290
00:15:21,350 --> 00:15:22,950
What the heck happened?

291
00:15:22,950 --> 00:15:25,110
What could have hurt you so badly?

292
00:15:25,110 --> 00:15:28,430
Well, now, where shall I begin?

293
00:15:28,430 --> 00:15:30,450
Hey, before that, just one thing...

294
00:15:30,990 --> 00:15:33,610
The alliance with Crusch-san is on.

295
00:15:33,610 --> 00:15:36,530
Now are you satisfied with the 
results you got from abandoning me?

296
00:15:36,780 --> 00:15:39,630
Yes, most satisfied.

297
00:15:39,630 --> 00:15:41,280
Truly, truly,

298
00:15:41,280 --> 00:15:44,160
you were the once-in-a-lifetime 
windfall I had long waited for.

299
00:15:44,160 --> 00:15:45,450
Oh, really?

300
00:15:46,200 --> 00:15:48,840
Roswaal, what is this place?

301
00:15:49,250 --> 00:15:53,600
Since we got here... no, since we 
made contact with the barrier...

302
00:15:54,030 --> 00:15:57,010
I've had this anxious feeling 
in my chest, and I can't relax.

303
00:15:57,490 --> 00:15:59,780
I've heard it called the "Sanctuary,"

304
00:16:00,180 --> 00:16:02,640
but it doesn't seem like one to me at all.

305
00:16:03,340 --> 00:16:04,700
In fact, it feels more like...

306
00:16:05,790 --> 00:16:07,610
The Witch's Graveyard?

307
00:16:07,610 --> 00:16:11,270
Does it seem to make far 
more sense to call it that?

308
00:16:12,400 --> 00:16:13,460
What do you mean?

309
00:16:14,000 --> 00:16:16,870
Exactly what I said, nothing more or less.

310
00:16:16,870 --> 00:16:22,870
This is where the Witch of Greed, 
Echidna, met her end long ago,

311
00:16:22,870 --> 00:16:26,080
and in my mind, it is worth 
calling a "Sanctuary."

312
00:16:27,100 --> 00:16:28,420
Echidna...

313
00:16:28,820 --> 00:16:29,750
Subaru?

314
00:16:30,800 --> 00:16:31,790
Are you all right?

315
00:16:33,760 --> 00:16:35,160
Yeah, I'm fine.

316
00:16:35,580 --> 00:16:39,180
And why are you overseeing a place 
with that kind of backstory?

317
00:16:39,440 --> 00:16:41,010
It's quite simple.

318
00:16:41,010 --> 00:16:45,560
This land has been overseen by the heads 
of the Mathers family for generations.

319
00:16:45,560 --> 00:16:48,600
Then the Mathers family and 
the Witch of Greed have—

320
00:16:48,600 --> 00:16:49,730
<i>Echidna</i>.

321
00:16:50,000 --> 00:16:50,690
Huh?

322
00:16:51,120 --> 00:16:54,690
Please, when you speak
of her, do use her name.

323
00:16:54,690 --> 00:16:58,980
The name "Witch of Greed" 
makes her sound so evil.

324
00:16:58,980 --> 00:17:00,950
That's not very nice, is it?

325
00:17:01,640 --> 00:17:06,330
Um, then... The Mathers family and Echidna 
have been acquainted for a long time,

326
00:17:06,610 --> 00:17:09,250
and that's why they've always 
overseen this place?

327
00:17:09,250 --> 00:17:13,440
Yes, though to say we "oversee" 
it is a bit of an exaggeration.

328
00:17:13,440 --> 00:17:15,400
Echidna's barrier prevents entry

329
00:17:15,400 --> 00:17:18,790
by outsiders who fail to follow 
the forest's proper procedure.

330
00:17:18,790 --> 00:17:22,570
In addition, the barrier has 
certain effects on those

331
00:17:22,570 --> 00:17:24,730
whose blood meets certain conditions.

332
00:17:25,350 --> 00:17:28,610
Did you not experience this 
yourself, Emilia-sama?

333
00:17:30,560 --> 00:17:34,440
And how did you end up in such a sorry state?

334
00:17:36,790 --> 00:17:39,660
Did you not find it at all strange, Emilia-sama?

335
00:17:40,010 --> 00:17:40,560
Huh?

336
00:17:41,080 --> 00:17:43,520
That all the people who fled to the Sanctuary,

337
00:17:43,520 --> 00:17:46,820
as well as Roswaal-sama
and myself, stayed here

338
00:17:46,820 --> 00:17:48,980
and didn't return to the mansion?

339
00:17:49,560 --> 00:17:50,870
Well...

340
00:17:50,870 --> 00:17:53,300
I mean, you stayed here 
because you're hurt, right?

341
00:17:54,240 --> 00:18:00,430
We are all being held under house 
arrest here in the Sanctuary.

342
00:18:00,430 --> 00:18:01,430
Huh?!

343
00:18:01,840 --> 00:18:05,360
Myself, Ram, and the people of Arlam...

344
00:18:05,360 --> 00:18:09,500
Oh, and you two as well, from the
 moment you entered here.

345
00:18:10,190 --> 00:18:13,220
The hell? You guys are still 
flappin' your gums in here?

346
00:18:13,220 --> 00:18:16,000
House arrest... Then are Roswaal's injuries...

347
00:18:16,000 --> 00:18:20,370
Nope. He got hurt 'cause he 
was rejected by the trial.

348
00:18:20,370 --> 00:18:21,290
Trial?

349
00:18:21,290 --> 00:18:22,370
What does that mean?

350
00:18:23,000 --> 00:18:27,980
You've seen what happens when you come 
in contact with the barrier, right?

351
00:18:28,670 --> 00:18:31,720
Mixed-bloods who go through 
that and still come in here

352
00:18:31,720 --> 00:18:34,090
are never allowed to leave.

353
00:18:35,460 --> 00:18:36,960
Does that mean Emilia, too?

354
00:18:38,140 --> 00:18:40,890
The barrier doesn't mean squat to most people.

355
00:18:40,890 --> 00:18:44,560
Doesn't that seem a little unfair, Emilia-sama?

356
00:18:45,540 --> 00:18:48,880
The only way to break the barrier is 
to go through the graveyard's trial,

357
00:18:48,880 --> 00:18:52,300
but if anyone who isn't a 
mixed-blood tries it...

358
00:18:54,800 --> 00:18:57,650
All the villagers are rounded up in one place.

359
00:18:57,650 --> 00:19:00,040
So long as they don't act up, we won't hurt 'em.

360
00:19:00,040 --> 00:19:01,780
They even get three meals 
and a nap every day!

361
00:19:03,260 --> 00:19:05,450
This is our demand.

362
00:19:05,870 --> 00:19:08,350
Break the barrier surrounding 
this Sanctuary.

363
00:19:08,350 --> 00:19:10,860
The only one allowed to undergo 
the trial to do that is you.

364
00:19:10,860 --> 00:19:14,570
If you can't break it, we won't 
let any of the villagers leave.

365
00:19:14,570 --> 00:19:18,700
Of course, you can't leave 
here yourself, either!

366
00:19:29,740 --> 00:19:30,960
Subaru-sama!

367
00:19:31,470 --> 00:19:32,690
Thank goodness you're safe!

368
00:19:32,690 --> 00:19:34,530
I'm glad you're all okay.

369
00:19:34,530 --> 00:19:36,310
Are the others all right?

370
00:19:36,310 --> 00:19:38,400
Is the lord recovering from his injuries?

371
00:19:38,790 --> 00:19:40,920
We heard he got hurt trying to help us.

372
00:19:39,210 --> 00:19:40,920
We're truly relieved!

373
00:19:41,310 --> 00:19:43,410
Okay, everyone, listen up.

374
00:19:43,630 --> 00:19:47,320
As you know, we got rid of the bad 
guy who attacked the village.

375
00:19:50,220 --> 00:19:52,420
The other group that evacuated

376
00:19:52,420 --> 00:19:55,320
is back at the village, waiting for
 all of you to come home.

377
00:19:57,000 --> 00:20:01,480
I guess you've all been informed that 
it's not easy to get out of here.

378
00:20:01,960 --> 00:20:03,220
But don't worry!

379
00:20:03,420 --> 00:20:08,160
We've got someone who's going to undergo 
the trial to set you all free!

380
00:20:08,160 --> 00:20:09,050
You mean...

381
00:20:09,050 --> 00:20:10,940
You're going to do it?

382
00:20:10,940 --> 00:20:14,380
No, if I could do it, I'd be 
more than happy to, but...

383
00:20:24,310 --> 00:20:26,030
I think you all know who this is.

384
00:20:26,030 --> 00:20:28,260
It's Emilia, the royal selection candidate.

385
00:20:28,260 --> 00:20:29,890
She'll be undergoing the trial.

386
00:20:32,550 --> 00:20:34,750
I-I'm sorry you had to wait so long.

387
00:20:35,070 --> 00:20:38,000
In the place of your domain lord,
Roswaal L. Mathers,

388
00:20:38,000 --> 00:20:39,710
I will undergo the trial.

389
00:20:40,990 --> 00:20:42,090
I would appreciate your support!

390
00:20:46,790 --> 00:20:49,380
Let me ask you just one thing.

391
00:20:49,380 --> 00:20:50,610
Chief...

392
00:20:50,610 --> 00:20:51,720
Why do this?

393
00:20:52,100 --> 00:20:56,600
You bowed your head to us the 
last time you saw us, too,

394
00:20:57,030 --> 00:21:01,440
but we were the ones who turned you away.

395
00:21:03,730 --> 00:21:08,350
If it's because you want us to 
back you in the royal selection,

396
00:21:08,350 --> 00:21:12,470
that's just fine, so long 
as you come out and say so.

397
00:21:13,600 --> 00:21:16,290
But if you have some other reason,

398
00:21:16,870 --> 00:21:18,600
we would like to know...

399
00:21:19,360 --> 00:21:25,470
that you are not a witch who 
is beyond our comprehension.

400
00:21:34,250 --> 00:21:40,130
I don't have the confidence to give 
you a respectable answer right now.

401
00:21:40,130 --> 00:21:45,780
I don't have any strong, convincing 
words that would satisfy all of you.

402
00:21:46,250 --> 00:21:47,030
But...

403
00:21:47,030 --> 00:21:51,320
Though it wasn't for very long, 
I spent a few days with your families,

404
00:21:51,320 --> 00:21:53,280
the ones who aren't here now.

405
00:21:53,280 --> 00:21:55,620
And it made me realize...

406
00:21:56,800 --> 00:21:59,750
that families should be together.

407
00:22:01,100 --> 00:22:05,360
I want to return all of you to your families.

408
00:22:05,360 --> 00:22:08,100
I didn't promise them that I'd do so...

409
00:22:08,960 --> 00:22:10,760
But I promised myself.

410
00:22:12,890 --> 00:22:15,350
That's my only reason.

411
00:22:16,750 --> 00:22:20,560
I wasn't really thinking about 
earning your support or anything.

412
00:22:21,490 --> 00:22:23,730
But if possible, I'd like to...

413
00:22:24,580 --> 00:22:25,390
um...

414
00:22:26,550 --> 00:22:28,080
be friends with you all.

415
00:22:28,080 --> 00:22:29,830
That's what I want.

416
00:22:33,430 --> 00:22:34,680
Emilia-sama...

417
00:22:34,680 --> 00:22:35,730
Y-Yes?

418
00:22:36,830 --> 00:22:40,120
I realize this will sound like we 
only care about what benefits us,

419
00:22:40,780 --> 00:22:41,940
but...

420
00:22:44,770 --> 00:22:47,010
I pray you will accept our friendship.

421
00:22:49,120 --> 00:22:50,660
P-Please, I should ask the same!

422
00:22:51,250 --> 00:22:52,760
I know I'm not worthy,

423
00:22:52,760 --> 00:22:54,010
but please accept my friendship!

424
00:22:54,830 --> 00:22:58,100
"I'm not worthy"? Who says 
that in this day and age?

425
00:23:00,080 --> 00:23:01,220
Emilia-sama...

426
00:23:02,510 --> 00:23:04,860
seems to have changed a bit.

427
00:23:06,280 --> 00:23:08,030
Is it because of something you said to her?

428
00:23:09,080 --> 00:23:11,520
It's the result of her thinking 
things through on her own.

429
00:23:11,520 --> 00:23:15,690
You shouldn't assume all her 
decisions come from someone else.

430
00:23:16,090 --> 00:23:16,980
You're right.

431
00:23:18,120 --> 00:23:19,660
I was in the wrong this time.

432
00:23:31,720 --> 00:23:35,260
Did you get enough support 
from the lesser spirits?

433
00:23:35,680 --> 00:23:37,310
Yeah. Everything's fine.

434
00:23:37,810 --> 00:23:40,530
Still, I think I'd like one last cheer.

435
00:23:40,530 --> 00:23:41,690
Can I do it?

436
00:23:42,230 --> 00:23:43,660
I want you to.

437
00:23:44,200 --> 00:23:45,020
Please.

438
00:23:45,600 --> 00:23:47,730
You can do it! Don't give up! EMC!

439
00:23:47,730 --> 00:23:50,420
Emilia-tan, major challenger!

440
00:23:51,960 --> 00:23:52,990
Thank you.

441
00:24:04,340 --> 00:24:07,970
That means she's been approved as a 
qualified challenger in the trial.

442
00:24:09,360 --> 00:24:10,250
I'm going now.

443
00:24:14,520 --> 00:24:16,890
I get that it sucks being trapped here.

444
00:24:17,770 --> 00:24:19,890
But why didn't you do this yourself?

445
00:24:21,640 --> 00:24:23,310
If I could, I would, damn it.

446
00:24:28,610 --> 00:24:31,110
H-Hey, is she gonna be okay?

447
00:24:31,320 --> 00:24:34,720
The light's not supposed to go out 
as long as the trial's going on...

448
00:24:34,720 --> 00:24:35,760
Emilia!

449
00:24:35,760 --> 00:24:36,240
Barusu!

450
00:24:40,850 --> 00:24:41,500
Why...

451
00:24:41,500 --> 00:24:44,640
I don't understand, but if I can get 
in there, that's good enough for me!

452
00:24:44,640 --> 00:24:47,840
Just stay there! I'll yell if I need you!

453
00:24:55,040 --> 00:24:56,070
Emilia!

454
00:24:57,880 --> 00:25:00,470
<i>First, you need to face your own past.</i>

455
00:25:14,240 --> 00:25:16,070
Good morning, son of mine!

456
00:25:17,570 --> 00:25:20,660
Hey, c'mon! What? What? What's wrong?

457
00:25:20,920 --> 00:25:24,750
You look as if you just saw your own 
dad naked first thing in the morning!

458
00:25:27,000 --> 00:25:30,000
The Long-Awaited Reunion

459
00:25:27,000 --> 00:25:37,000


